## SECTION 2: MARKET REGIME DETECTION (Run First — Non-Negotiable)

Skipping regime detection collapses win rate. A great setup in a bear market is a trap.

### 2.1 Regime Logic (based on SPY daily data)

| Condition | Regime | Bias | Size Multiplier |
|---|---|---|---|
| SPY > SMA200 AND SMA50 > SMA200 AND SMA50 slope > 0 | BULL | Long | 1.0x |
| SPY < SMA200 AND SMA50 < SMA200 | BEAR | Avoid longs / short rallies | 0.5x |
| Otherwise | NEUTRAL | Long-light (RS leaders only) | 0.7x |

### 2.2 VIX Overlay (applied on top of regime)

| VIX Level | Interpretation | Additional Size Adjustment |
|---|---|---|
| VIX < 18 | Low fear, full sizing OK | 1.0x |
| VIX 18–25 | Normal, standard sizing | 1.0x |
| VIX 25–30 | Elevated fear | 0.75x |
| VIX > 30 | High fear, reduce all | 0.5x |
| VIX > 35 | Extreme — consider standing aside | 0.25x |

### 2.3 Regime Action Table

| Regime | VIX | Action |
|---|---|---|
| Bull | < 18 | Full size, target breakouts and pullbacks |
| Bull | 18–25 | Normal size, prefer pullback entries |
| Bull | > 25 | Half size, widen stops, take profits sooner |
| Neutral | Any | 70% size, highest-RS stocks only |
| Bear | Any | Stay out of longs or short rallies, reduce exposure |

