## SECTION 3: UNIVERSE & LIQUIDITY FILTERS (Hard Binary Filters)

Fail any filter → ticker is immediately dropped. No exceptions.

### Starting Universe
- S&P 500 components (via Wikipedia or data provider)
- Nasdaq 100 (higher beta, better for momentum)
- Optionally: sector ETFs for macro plays

### Hard Filters

| Filter | Threshold | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| Price | $10 – $500 | Avoid penny stocks and extremely high-priced shares |
| Avg daily volume (20-day) | >= 1,000,000 shares | Liquidity for entry/exit without slippage |
| Dollar volume (20-day avg) | >= $10,000,000/day | Ensures real turnover |
| Market cap | >= $1B | Avoid micro-caps with erratic behavior |
| Earnings distance | No earnings within 5–7 trading days | Avoid binary gap risk |

