## SECTION 4: INDICATOR CALCULATIONS

Compute all on daily OHLCV bars. Minimum 60 bars required per ticker.

### 4.1 Trend Indicators
- SMA(20), SMA(50), SMA(200): price relationship to each confirms trend direction
- EMA(20): faster-reacting; used for pullback proximity detection
- ADX(14): measures trend strength regardless of direction; > 20 = trending, > 25 = strong
- SMA(50) slope: (SMA50[today] / SMA50[10 bars ago]) - 1 × 100 → positive = healthy trend

### 4.2 Momentum Indicators
- RSI(14): target zone 45–70 for longs; above 50 = bullish, below 70 = not overbought
- MACD histogram (12,26,9): positive and rising = momentum building

### 4.3 Volatility Indicators
- ATR(14): average true range; raw value and as % of close
- ATR% = ATR(14) / Close × 100 → target band: 2% – 8% (fuel gauge)
- Bollinger Band Bandwidth = (BB_upper - BB_lower) / BB_midline → low = squeeze

### 4.4 Volume Indicators
- RVOL = Volume[today] / Volume.rolling(20).mean() → > 1.5x = institutional interest
- OBV = cumsum(sign(close.diff()) × volume) → rising = accumulation
- OBV slope = (OBV[-1] - OBV[-10]) / abs(OBV[-10]) × 100 → positive = buying pressure

### 4.5 Relative Strength vs Benchmark (SPY)
- RS_Nd = stock_return_Nd - SPY_return_Nd for N = 20, 60, 120 days
- Stock must be in top 20–30% of universe by RS on at least 1 window
- Positive RS on all 3 windows = true leader, not just riding the market

### 4.6 Key Formulas
```
ATR%     = ATR(14) / Close × 100
RVOL     = Volume / rolling_mean(Volume, 20)
RS_Nd    = pct_change(close, N) - pct_change(spy_close, N)
OBV      = cumsum(sign(diff(close)) × volume)
BB_bw    = (BB_upper - BB_lower) / BB_midline
SMA50_slope = (SMA50[-1] / SMA50[-10] - 1) × 100
```

