## SECTION 6: COMPOSITE SCORING SYSTEM

After hard filters, many tickers survive. Score ranks them by probability quality.

Each component is normalized 0.0–1.0, multiplied by weight, summed, multiplied by 100.

### Scoring Weights

| Component | Weight | How to Score 1.0 |
|---|---|---|
| Trend alignment | 20% | All 5 trend conditions met (price > SMA20 > SMA50 > SMA200, ADX > 20) |
| Pattern quality | 20% | Clean breakout/pullback with tight base, high RVOL, ideal RSI |
| Relative strength | 15% | Outperforms SPY on all 3 windows (1M, 3M, 6M) |
| Relative volume | 12% | RVOL > 3x (strong institutional volume surge) |
| RSI alignment | 10% | RSI near 60 (early continuation zone, not overbought) |
| Risk:Reward | 10% | R:R > 5:1 |
| ATR% fit | 8% | ATR% near 4.5% (ideal swing volatility) |
| OBV slope | 5% | OBV rising over last 10 days |

Composite = sum(component × weight) × 100

### Regime Multiplier (applied after composite score)
- Bull regime: × 1.1
- Neutral: × 1.0
- Bear: × 0.6
- VIX > 30: additional × 0.8

Score thresholds:
- Score >= 60: Strong candidate — investigate seriously
- Score 45–59: Moderate — only if chart structure is clean
- Score < 45: Weak — avoid

