## SECTION 7: RISK MANAGEMENT & POSITION SIZING

Every trade requires three numbers set BEFORE execution: entry, stop, target.
If R:R < 2:1 → reject the trade regardless of how the chart looks.

### 7.1 Stop Placement by Pattern
- Breakout: below the base low (the support that just held)
- Pullback: 1.0–1.5 × ATR(14) below the entry candle
- Squeeze: below the most recent swing low

### 7.2 Target Calculation
- First target: prior swing high (known supply zone)
- Second target: measured move = base_height + breakout_point
- Never place target at round numbers — use price structure only

### 7.3 Position Sizing Formula
```
dollar_risk    = account_size × risk_pct_per_trade    (e.g., $1000 × 0.01 = $10)
risk_per_share = entry_price - stop_price
shares         = floor(dollar_risk / risk_per_share)
position_value = shares × entry_price
max_rr         = (target - entry) / (entry - stop)    # must be >= 2.0
```

### 7.4 Position Size Table

| Account | Risk/Trade | Dollar Risk | Example |
|---|---|---|---|
| $1,000 | 1% | $10 | Buy $50 stock, stop $49 → 10 shares max |
| $5,000 | 1% | $50 | Buy $50 stock, stop $47 → 17 shares max |
| $10,000 | 1% | $100 | Buy $50 stock, stop $45 → 20 shares max |
| $25,000 | 1% | $250 | Buy $50 stock, stop $45 → 50 shares max |

### 7.5 Portfolio Risk Rules
1. Never risk more than 1–2% of account on any single trade
2. Never hold more than 4–5 open positions simultaneously
3. Total portfolio risk (all open positions combined) must not exceed 5–8%
4. R:R below 2:1 = reject, even if chart looks perfect

